{"name":"Firecracker","hex":"#f2643a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"firecracker","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small explosive device, typically containing a small amount of gunpowder in a tightly-wound roll of paper, primarily designed to produce a large bang.","A peanut butter cracker baked with marijuana, similar in concept to an Alice B. Toklas brownie."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/firecracker"}],"entries":[{"title":"Firecracker","blocks":[{"text":"A firecracker is a small explosive device primarily designed to produce a large amount of noise, especially in the form of a loud bang, usually for celebration or entertainment; any visual effect is incidental to this goal. They have fuses, and are wrapped in a heavy paper casing to contain the explosive compound. Firecrackers, along with fireworks, originated in China."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Firecrackers.png/330px-Firecrackers.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firecracker"},{"title":"Firecracker (Lisa Loeb album)","blocks":[{"text":"Firecracker is the second solo studio album by Lisa Loeb. It was released in 1997 through Geffen Records. Its cover features original artwork by illustrator Mark Miller, who transposed Loeb on to one of his original artworks, \"Kitten\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/40/LisaLoeb_Firecracker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firecracker_(Lisa_Loeb_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Beautiful_large_flower_cracker_creating_brilliant_light_and_sparkles_at_night.jpg/500px-Beautiful_large_flower_cracker_creating_brilliant_light_and_sparkles_at_night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia